@article{sun2026granularity,
  title   = {The Score Granularity Gap in Black-Box {LLM} Classification: A Comparative Study of Confidence Constructions},
  author  = {Sun, Ao and Sun, Tian and Geng, Jiaxing},
  journal = {arXiv preprint arXiv:2606.22179},
  year    = {2026},
  annote  = {THE precedent for our granularity argument. Shows verbalized confidence "ranks cases surprisingly well, yet takes only a handful of distinct values", so it "offers an operator only a few coarse thresholds, no matter how well it ranks" — i.e. granularity upper-bounds operational controllability independently of ranking quality. We CITE rather than claim this. WHAT WE INSTANTIATE IT WITH, CORRECTED 2026-08-13: this annote previously offered "22 distinct values across 97 questions" as our instance. BOTH quantities are retired. (i) 22 was a REALISED distinct-value count, which is monotone in the number of targets scored — E[realised] for a random 80 from the same stratum is 23.0, so 22 is the 37th percentile, and the same population gives 28 at n=200 and 35 at n=2000; it measured the sample, not the estimator (critique_log entry 33 sec.4, commit e6e7629). (ii) The 97 denominator pooled the complete 80-target false-alarm arm with a hide arm truncated mid-campaign at 17, so it was stale by construction and has been purged from the paper (commit 5d822b9). Our surviving instance is the n-invariant ATTAINABLE lattice: 39 values at N=10 (the partitions of 10), of which only 2 lie in the top tenth of the range — the region a false alarm must reach — plus the residue that N=20 lifts the top decile only from 2 points to 7. Distinguish on setting: theirs is black-box LLM CLASSIFICATION with verbalized confidence over 25 model-dataset pairs; ours is a sampling-based generative detector whose score is an entropy over answer clusters, where the granularity limit is imposed by the sample budget N. Title/authors verified on arXiv 2026-08-11. SCOOP-CHECK RESOLVED: the sweep reported that they explicitly exclude generative settings, which is not visible in the abstract and we have not page-verified. Nothing in the paper depends on it — Intro and Related Work claim only that we instantiate their argument for a sampling-based generative detector, which requires no assertion about what their scope excludes. Do NOT reintroduce a "they leave our cell open" phrasing without reading the full text.}
}

