@article{pan2026shade,
  title   = {Mind the Unseen Mass: Unmasking LLM Hallucinations via Soft-Hybrid Alphabet Estimation},
  author  = {Pan, Hongxing and Guo, Yingying and Kuang, Wenqing and Lu, Jiashi},
  journal = {arXiv preprint arXiv:2604.19162},
  year    = {2026},
  annote  = {Title/authors/date/abstract VERIFIED by me on arXiv 2026-08-12 (submitted 21 Apr 2026). Same strand as mccabe2025alphabet and a more recent instance: "frequency-based estimators tend to undercount rare semantic modes when the sample size is small", corrected via Good-Turing coverage plus a heat-kernel trace of an entailment-weighted graph, yielding a "coverage-adjusted semantic entropy score". TWO uses for us. (a) It reinforces contribution (1)'s reconciliation: an estimator capped at log N must understate, and here is a second group correcting that understatement. (b) It is a concrete instance of the rebuttal our Discussion already anticipates -- "use an estimator with more range" CONCEDES the measurement point rather than refuting it; someone has now built that estimator. VERIFIED NOT to discuss discreteness or granularity (few distinct attainable values). SCOOP-CHECK CONCLUSION REWRITTEN 2026-08-13: this annote previously concluded that it does not scoop "our distinct-value / non-relaxability strand, which remains distinct". BOTH HALVES OF THAT STRAND ARE NOW DEAD, so there is no longer a strand for it to scoop. (i) "Only 22 distinct values" is RETIRED (critique_log entry 33 sec.4, commit e6e7629): a realised distinct-value count is monotone in the number of targets scored -- E[distinct] for a random 80 from the same stratum is 23.0, so the observed 22 is the 37th percentile, and the same population gives 28 at n=200 and 35 at n=2000. It was a sample size, not an estimator property. (ii) NON-RELAXABILITY is WITHDRAWN AS FALSE (critique_log entry 33 sec.3, commit 4683e26): the attainable lattice is 39 values at N=10 and 455 at N=20, so granularity is relaxable by ~12x -- and, per defect (2) of that entry, the mechanism we had claimed for it ("the baseline rises with the cap") IS the plug-in negative-bias decay that THIS paper and mccabe2025alphabet describe, i.e. it was their result all along. What we retain is narrower: the n-invariant lattice (39 attainable values at N=10, only 2 of them in the top tenth of the range) as an INSTANTIATION for a sampling-based generative detector of the granularity argument sun2026granularity already made for black-box classification, plus the residue that N=20 lifts the top decile only from 2 points to 7. Against that narrowed claim this paper still does not scoop us -- it corrects the UNDERSTATEMENT (coverage-adjusted magnitude), never the DISCRETENESS -- but the non-overlap is now much smaller than this annote used to assert, and uses (a) and (b) above are the load-bearing reasons to cite it.}
}

